 follow his fixation with ichigo and  orihime stem from that very real desire  to understand humans to comprehend the  power of emotions they held within and  just as he's on the road to redemption  that door gets promptly shut on him it's  just a perfect way to end what i feel is  one of the most hyped fights in that arc  up next it's a man sucking on a pacifier  wearing a bonnet diaper and big  [Music]  despite his sunglasses and his girl gang  who insists he's hard-boiled which i  assume is the reason why he's such a hit  with the ladies  it's impossible to take this big belly  man child seriously at first but it  turns out the story behind that  ridiculous outfit isn't just serious  it's seriously sad  senora pink's clownish appearance is a  tribute to his dead son one that he puts  on for his wife russian with their  relationship already strained by their  son's death russian leaves pink upon  finding out that he's a pirate and not a  banker as he claims to be she's then  involved in an accident and ends up in a  vegetative state a shattered pink visits  her in hospital every day one day on  impulse he puts on a baby bonnet to coax  a smile out of her to his great surprise  he succeeds and that's the beginning of  his transformation a man brave enough to  be ridiculed by all for the smallest  reward and the briefest moment of  happiness has our respect  is up next in our rogues gallery of  tragic shonen villains  curiosity kill the cat is what i'd use  to describe zeref's downfall in this  world there are some things that we're  not meant to know and zereth just had to  have the curiosity to deal with life  itself it led to a curse one that would  begin his downward spiral zero for me is  a character whose reputation precedes  the truth about him for most of the  series he's been billed as this super  villain the ultimate dark wizard who  would end the world something like that  so i was excited to see him finally  confront the heroes quite early on in  the series only to have my expectations  subverted heck if anything it was  aknologia who fits the bill of the evil  destroyer more as the story of fairy  tale unfolds there have since become a  death seeker looking for atonement in  his endless trudge across the world  various legends that tell of his evil  have indeed been born but beyond all  these scary tales lies a broken man i  mean seeing everyone you ever cared for  die will take a toll on anyone and that  includes one of the most powerful  wizards in the world  we move on from battle shonen to look at  isabella  what lies beyond that firm facade of a  strong woman one who hides a very  sinister knowledge underneath her warm  smile as one of the best caretakers of  the grace field house tragedy  lots of it let's see isabella started  out quite the optimist like a lot of  them one of the best mom candidates she  reached that goal with record-breaking  feats however it's not without pain and  suffering and on route to claiming the  title of being the youngest mother of  them all she's lost so much in her  struggle to survive her new role does  open her up to the whole demon farming  system that's plagued these houses but  as if the tragedy of the system she's  trapped in isn't enough she gets privy  to another gut-wrenching truth one of  the children she's raising up to be fed  is none other than her own son for most  of the first season of the promised  neverland you see isabella as the cold  unflinching war that the children can't  ever seem to overcome a powerful  adversary who's overcome everything  thrown at her even attempts at  usurpation from a fellow colleague but  the end of it all shocks us with a twist  that gives a completely new perspective  to her character the promise neverland  season one is truly one of the best  anime had to offer in its year  i think it's about time to take a half  time break if you've enjoyed what you've  seen so far don't hesitate to subscribe  we're trying to get to that one million  subscriber milestone and we just need a  little bit more of a push to finally hit  that mark  [Music]  we resume the list with marouane  honestly  [Music]  i think it's not an unpopular opinion  that meruem is one of the best shonen  villains there is he may not have the  grandiose charisma of some of the most  broken ones like aizen or mardara but in  terms of character writing and  development he's just on par with the  rest of hunter hunter in terms of  execution i won't say that he  single-handedly carried the kimura  antarc but he sure as hell played a  crucial role in the arc being as awesome  as it was i'm not gonna lie his batter  with natero is a thing of legend there's  a lot to say about meruem that can  become a character study altogether like  how he's such a great foil for gone  despite not interacting with him spoiler  for a future video there maybe  but the moment that i'd love to focus on  for the sake of this video is his moment  of death don't lie that final moment  with gomugi should have made you shed a  tear at least he came into the series by  making an impact as a detestable villain  but we eventually see those traces of  cruelty crumble through these  interactions with others over the course  of an arc by the time he dies he's  become one of the best characters in  shonen anime a very honorable one of  that like all kiara he has his most  touching moments right at death's  doorstep closing the doors on one of my  favorite anime villains of all time  next up is hitachi  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  i expect this to be the most polarizing  character that i picked for this list  much has been said about hitachi or the  uchihas in general trust me for those of  you who weren't around back then the  discussion on itachi's actions were a  remarkable sight i'd say it's on par  with a lot of ship wars or political  discussions in terms of intensity so was  hitachi a tragic hero all along was his  role in the whole massacre completely  justified  personally  i'm leaning towards no but  i do think that what's come out of his  actions is nothing short of tragic and  it's through those effects that feel bad  for him while he may have done some  reprehensible things he's proved that  things aren't as black and white as they  typically presented heck his actions  drove a little edgy brother to a whole  path of revenge when the true story  would quickly shatter sasuke's very  purpose for pursuing revenge and he had  to carry that burden with him all  throughout his run in the show all while  engaging in confrontations against  sasuke and fighting for his life you  could say what you want but the amount  of emotional baggage hitachi had to  carry was pretty insane the revelation  of the truth and his final sacrifice  makes his fight against sasuke even more  dramatic  and it's quickly become one of my  favorites ever since it first aired  following itachi we have shigaraki  [Music]  now this is a backstory that can really  hurt people on a personal level there's  nothing more painful than having a  father who just can't have it in him to  support your dreams as a child that's  some emotional scars that you just don't  recover from which makes the whole  shigeraki thing even more of a tragedy  we could have had a hero with such an  overpowered ability if only he had the  proper emotional support that a child  desperately needed from a father but  alas it wasn't meant to be and watching  shigaraki's whole story unfold was  something that severely tugged at my  heartstrings more than sadness for the  poor aspiring hero there was the sense  of frustration a sense of anger at the  father who was the reason for the child  to grow into the diabolical shigeraki  that we all know today in the name of  anger and bitterness at the world  shigaraki has done a lot of unforgivable  deeds what do you think about it can you  blame him for the path to villainy well  it's the bad guys who managed to show  t